# Catch-up runtime state: the watermark and the queue of missed customers. Per-deployment
# state, never source — committing it would hand another machine's watermark to this one
# and silently skip a real backlog.
apps/bot/src/data/meta.json
apps/bot/src/data/catchup_queue.json
# Admin console accounts: password hashes, sign-in token hashes, and who-did-what. Secrets
# per deployment — never commit.
apps/bot/src/data/admin_users.json
apps/bot/src/data/admin_roles.json
apps/bot/src/data/admin_sessions.json
apps/bot/src/data/admin_activity.json
# Runtime state that the RUNNING BOT writes, untracked 2026-09-22. Tracking these broke every
# deploy: `git pull` refuses to touch a file the server has modified, and the server modifies
# all of them just by working -- the first attempt to ship the 2026-09-22 update died on
# "Your local changes to apps/bot/src/data/products_cache.json would be overwritten by merge".
#
# ⚠️ On a JSON install (no MONGODB_URI) these files ARE the production database. Never
# `git checkout` or `git reset --hard` this directory on a server without backing it up first
# -- customers.json and tickets.json are real customers and real open tickets. db.js recreates
# any that are missing on boot, so a fresh clone starting empty is correct.
#
# Committing them was also quietly publishing customer phone numbers to the repo.
apps/bot/src/data/customers.json
apps/bot/src/data/tickets.json
apps/bot/src/data/retry_queue.json
apps/bot/src/data/knowledge_sources.json
apps/bot/src/data/knowledge_chunks.json
# Regenerated by `npm run sync`. products_cache.seed.json IS tracked and is the fallback when
# this file is absent -- see getLocalProducts(). Without that seed a fresh clone has no
# catalogue at all, which matters here because the store's REST API has been blocked for
# weeks at a time (see "WooCommerce REST blocked" in CLAUDE.md).
apps/bot/src/data/products_cache.json
apps/bot/public/invoices/*.pdf
.wwebjs_auth/
.wwebjs_cache/
scratch/
test_gemini_tools.js
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
.DS_Store
# Cached ONNX embedding model (~30MB, re-downloaded from the HF hub on first use)
.models/

# Admin console build outputs.
# `dist/` is the Vercel build — Vercel builds it on every deploy, so it is never committed.
# `dist-express/` IS committed: it is the base:'/admin/' build the bot's Express server
# serves as the self-hosted fallback, and the deploy box runs `npm ci --omit=dev` with no
# dev dependencies, so it cannot build it itself.
apps/admin/dist/
.vercel/

# SSH deploy keypair — never commit
Aurax
Aurax.pub
